codex
This isolation removed the auxiliary recursive-call circularity the whole-module theorem legitimately depends on, so the backend is unrolling recursion rather than testing the original dependency graph. I’ll stop this diagnostic if it remains nonterminal, retain the log, and use a labeled two-claim copy to select the target while preserving its proved helper.
